.TH "HTMLTEXTAREAELEMENT.SELECTIONCHANGE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTextAreaElement.selectionchange_event \- HTMLTextAreaElement:
selectionchange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]selectionchange\f[B]\f[R] event of the Selection API is
fired when the text selection within a \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] element is
changed in either extent or direction, whether the selection is a caret
or a range of characters.
.PP
For general information about this event, see
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R]: \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqselectionchange\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onselectionchange = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
